# Docker build context exclusions for the `frontend` image.
#
# The root `.dockerignore` does NOT apply here: the frontend service builds with
# `context: ./frontend`, and Docker only reads a `.dockerignore` at the root of
# the context it is given. Without this file the ~1.5 GB `node_modules` and
# `src-tauri/target` trees would be uploaded to the daemon on every build.

# ── Dependencies and build output (all regenerated inside the image) ──────────
node_modules
.next
out
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── The desktop shell ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `src-tauri/` is the Tauri Rust backend. The web image never compiles it, and
# `src-tauri/target/` alone is several GB. Excluding it is the single largest
# saving in this file.
src-tauri

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never let a local `.env.local` reach the image; the container gets its
# configuration from compose at build time (NEXT_PUBLIC_*) and run time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Tests and tooling (not needed to produce a production bundle) ────────────
tests
playwright-report
test-results
coverage
vitest.config.ts
playwright.config.ts
**/__tests__

# ── Local noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
*.log
.DS_Store
